{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-topology-points}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-topological-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:086b218376c2256e72d0bf662883ce927920be3259d3f5b50e6eedd6163817ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ee70c625d51f27f3444a4848457c2ccaaf69b9add2502c0e8cfed97db25f53bf", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nThe underlying <TEXTITOPEN_0001>topological space<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> is the set of points\n<MATH_0003> endowed with the topology constructed in\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e194125b06299a63c0c4623f19158ca1e6eb75c7225ddf2e22da7950b54ceee", "unit_id": "tag:04Y8:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e0969af30ca794ee81c1f1e8930b5eb963f2c0bf12460f9070a69b1739c5ef99", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ba52be0def66f14bcabdedc463e90660dca5038a02420397f02a9287c6893d33", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis definition does not conflict with the already existing topology\non <MATH_0001> if <MATH_0002> is an algebraic space.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1ec42c59790a73204f55e814878ea5c823254762e5899ed5b1eec1e62f04a8eb", "unit_id": "tag:04XE:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-locally-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-space-locally-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e1bfbeeba06a94115f284b0e7ed69a47616aa6bcfa37478556cfbca0e58052d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:67f84f1db4c7e442940e81f68806438580628acbb410e83fe37bb27d94594f50", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nEvery point of <MATH_0002> has a fundamental system of\nquasi-compact open neighbourhoods.\nIn particular <MATH_0003> is locally quasi-compact in the sense of\nTopology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:812d66bf683f1f7e28f7d5782fb7f6f800ca2ace34f37d3e40431c553a35174c", "unit_id": "tag:04Y9:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$|U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-topology-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b4187fdad8e062992ee0728d217f51dca4e06628cd040592171629d1c4ee1f40", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9bd56c0d0135624e98b61131eaad5b60ec3ba9ed02b802852d5d8fdb0b0096e5", "source_text": "This follows formally from the fact that there exists a scheme\n<MATH_0001> and a surjective, open, continuous map <MATH_0002>\nof topological spaces. Namely, if <MATH_0003> is surjective and\nsmooth, then\nLemma <REF_0001>\nguarantees that <MATH_0004> is continuous, surjective, and open.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1d979c395f09e0bdaf8c6230a756e17b4aed5f7f2ea3eb5f766e5cf53fe7946", "unit_id": "tag:04Y9:proof"}
